# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# EAS only derives the archive from .gitignore when the project root is also the
# git root. Here it is not - eas.json lives in app/ and the repository starts one
# level up - so eas-cli copies the directory instead and .gitignore is not
# consulted. Without this file the archive was 984 MB: android/ (3.5 GB) and
# node_modules/ (3.3 GB) went up with it.
#
# .easignore REPLACES .gitignore for the archive rather than adding to it, so
# everything that must stay out has to be listed here, even if .gitignore already
# covers it.

# Installed on the build server from the lockfile.
node_modules/

# Generated by prebuild. Uploading it is actively harmful: EAS treats a project
# that already has android/ as bare and skips prebuild, so it would build this
# stale local tree - Gradle caches, .cxx output and an 82 MB APK included -
# instead of generating one from app.json and the config plugins.
/android
/ios

# Local native module build output. modules/ itself is source and must ship:
# autolinking reads it and the usage-stats module lives there.
modules/*/android/build/
modules/*/android/.cxx/
modules/*/android/.gradle/

# Local tooling and caches.
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
.kotlin/
.metro-health-check*
*.tsbuildinfo
.claude/
.vscode/

# Never upload signing material. EAS stores the keystore server-side; a stray
# copy in the archive would be one more place for it to leak from.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
*.pem

# Local env and logs.
.env*.local
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# OS noise.
.DS_Store
